    pr_ref:  # 60df
    description: "FOUND by WI-tusad F3 (live sweep, f3/live/sweep2.py, dev 3c9f03a81f). Perl block-form packages (`package A { sub go { 1 } }` then `package B { sub go { 2 } }`, Perl 5.14+) emit B's sub as `A::go`: the analyzer applies the package seen earlier in the file, not the block the sub sits in. Observed via `hypergumbo run`: nodes module A (1), function A::go (2), function A::go (5), module B (4). Consequences: wrong name/qualified identity for every sub in a later block package; the two subs tie and the per-file split numbers them, so blanking package A renames the survivor to `B::go` (it does not match its own earlier record). Fix: read the enclosing package_statement block (ancestor) for a sub, falling back to the latest statement-form `package X;` only outside blocks. Statement-form packages were not checked for a regression."  # 60df
    fields: {}  # 60df
